# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and loaded automatically by
# nfl_mcp/server.py at import time. Real environment variables always win, so
# container/CI values are never overwritten by this file.

# Live Vegas lines, spreads and implied team totals.
# Free tier: https://the-odds-api.com (500 credits/month, no credit card).
# One fetch = regions=us x markets=spreads,totals = 2 credits, so ~250 fetches
# per month. Lines are cached for 2 hours, which keeps usage well inside that.
# Without this key the Vegas tools fall back to neutral placeholder values.
ODDS_API_KEY=

# Optional server tuning (defaults shown).
# NFL_MCP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# NFL_MCP_PORT=9000
# NFL_MCP_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# NFL_MCP_PREFETCH=0
# NFL_MCP_PREFETCH_INTERVAL=900
# NFL_MCP_PREFETCH_NEWS=1
# NFL_MCP_PREFETCH_NEWS_INTERVAL=2700

# --- Data sources & terms ----------------------------------------------------
# Every source is free and on by default; the server is meant for personal,
# low-volume use. External sources: Sleeper (API), ESPN (site / core / fantasy
# news JSON), NBC Sports / Rotoworld (player news, HTML; RSS fallback), CBS
# Sports (player news, projections, expert picks; HTML), NFL.com (official
# practice report, HTML), nflverse (GitHub release files), FantasyCalc (API),
# The Odds API (needs ODDS_API_KEY above), Open-Meteo (weather API).
# Some of these sites' terms of use restrict automated access; read them and
# switch off what you do not want. Requests are rate limited per host
# (NFL_MCP_<API>_RATE_LIMIT, requests/minute, e.g. NFL_MCP_NBC_RATE_LIMIT=3;
# NBC defaults to 6/min to keep its robots.txt crawl delay of 10 s), paths
# robots.txt disallows are not used, and a failing news source backs off
# (30 min doubling to 12 h) -- see GET /health -> data_freshness.news.
#
# News sources (espn_fantasy, nbc, cbs). One line switches them:
#   NFL_MCP_NEWS_SOURCES=-nbc          every source but NBC
#   NFL_MCP_NEWS_SOURCES=-nbc,-cbs     ESPN only
#   NFL_MCP_NEWS_SOURCES=espn_fantasy  the same, as an allow list
#   NFL_MCP_NEWS_SOURCES=none          no news polling
# NFL_MCP_NEWS_SOURCES=espn_fantasy,nbc,cbs
